# Symlink to shared prompts directory (machine-local path)
prompts
# ...but the AI-review prompt corpus is deliberately published provenance
# (verbatim workflow script + originating request, abs-paths genericized).
!_ai/review/prompts/
!_ai/review/prompts/**
# ...and so is the powerlaw-decay reproducible prompt pair (owner design
# 2026-07-14; MyST-excluded from the built site, committed for provenance).
!theory/powerlaw-decay/prompts/
!theory/powerlaw-decay/prompts/**

# Symlink to sibling RAG repo (machine-local path)
HARK_ask-your-project
# Symlinks to sibling repos used during AI/RAG tooling work; their
# contents are NOT part of BufferStockTheory and must not be committed
# into this repo's history.
matsya
bellman-ddsl

# Specstory directory (AI development tool)
.specstory/

# LaTeX-to-MyST pipeline source now lives in BufferStockTheory-make/tools/build-myst/.
# This repo (-Latest) only receives the pipeline's outputs at _build/myst/
# (covered by the `_build/*` rule below) and the committed BufferStockTheory.md
# at repo root.
**/__pycache__/
# myst owns _build/ (mystmd hardcodes this path for `myst build --html`
# output and intermediates). Non-MyST artifacts live elsewhere now:
# AI-comprehension renders in _ai/, PDF-bisect snapshots in _bisect/.
_build/*

# AI-comprehension artifacts (concept atlas renders, future glossary
# exports, etc.). The concept-atlas render output is committed (regenerated
# by tools/concepts_render.py); the recursive `**` exception auto-tracks
# any future files written under _ai/concepts/ (graph dumps, JSON-LD, etc.).
_ai/*
!_ai/concepts/
!_ai/concepts/**
# The _ai/ index README documents the tracked concepts/audit/review subtrees;
# track it too so the atlas entry point is versioned with what it indexes.
!_ai/README.md

# PDF-equivalence regression-bisect snapshots (worktrees + per-step PDFs
# + run logs). Generated by tools/private/bisect_pdf.sh; never tracked.
_bisect/*

# git worktree on the gh-pages branch, materialized by `make myst-publish`
# (BufferStockTheory-make/scripts/myst-publish.sh). Removable via
# `make myst-publish-clean`. The worktree is its own git checkout — never
# tracked from the parent repo.
_gh-pages/
